@page "/not-found"

@*
    The @page directive above is load-bearing, and not for the reason it looks.

    Routes.razor names this component as the router's NotFoundPage, and .NET 10's Router
    validates that eagerly in SetParametersAsync: a type with no RouteAttribute throws
    before the router renders anything at all. Without it the app does not fail to show a
    404, it fails to start, and the symptom is a boot spinner that never resolves.

    RoutesTests covers this.
*@

<PageTitle>Not found</PageTitle>

<h1>Nothing here</h1>
<p class="muted">That screen does not exist. Everything EleFi can do is on the tabs below.</p>
